WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.388 --> 00:00:14.209
was so happy he couldn't sleep!

2
00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:16.750
Tomorrow was his first day of school.

3
00:00:17.551 --> 00:00:19.792
He thought about the wonderful things he would learn.

4
00:00:20.492 --> 00:00:25.554
When the sun came up, he jumped out of bed, grabbed his new book, and ran off to

5
00:00:25.594 --> 00:00:28.575
school. "Bye, Father!"

6
00:00:29.076 --> 00:00:29.536
he shouted.

7
00:00:32.292 --> 00:00:34.714
Pinocchio talked to himself happily as he walked.

8
00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:37.055
"Today, I will learn to read.

9
00:00:37.536 --> 00:00:39.597
Tomorrow, I will learn to write.

10
00:00:40.198 --> 00:00:43.240
And the day after tomorrow, I will learn math.

11
00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.541
I will be so smart!

12
00:00:48.063 --> 00:00:51.466
I will be smart enough to get a job and earn money.

13
00:00:52.366 --> 00:00:54.268
I will buy Father a new coat.

14
00:00:54.948 --> 00:01:00.072
It will be a beautiful coat of green silk with diamond buttons.

15
00:01:00.992 --> 00:01:04.114
He was very kind to sell his coat for this book."

16
00:01:05.014 --> 00:01:07.876
As he talked to himself, he heard music in the distance.

17
00:01:10.697 --> 00:01:15.800
He walked toward the music and saw a crowd, a brightly colored tent, and a large sign.

18
00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:20.203
"Oh! I wish I didn't have to go to school today!

19
00:01:20.663 --> 00:01:24.245
This looks like so much fun," complained Pinocchio.

20
00:01:24.925 --> 00:01:26.986
Already, he had forgotten Geppetto's coat.

21
00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:31.792
"Excuse me," Pinocchio said to one of the villagers.

22
00:01:31.812 --> 00:01:33.973
"What does that sign say?"

23
00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:36.894
"Why? Can't you read?"

24
00:01:39.274 --> 00:01:40.775
the villager asked, laughing.

25
00:01:42.255 --> 00:01:44.856
"No," said Pinocchio, embarrassed.

26
00:01:46.356 --> 00:01:50.197
"It says 'Fettuccini's Marionette Theater, four lire.'

27
00:01:51.158 --> 00:01:52.918
The show starts in five minutes.

28
00:01:53.478 --> 00:01:54.759
But you can't read.

29
00:01:55.179 --> 00:01:56.499
You should be in school."

30
00:01:56.519 --> 00:01:59.660
"I don't want to go to school!"

31
00:02:00.128 --> 00:02:01.008
Pinocchio cried.

32
00:02:01.028 --> 00:02:04.369
"Do you have four lire I can borrow?"

33
00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:07.230
Pinocchio was embarrassed to beg.

34
00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:09.731
But he really wanted to see the show.

35
00:02:09.751 --> 00:02:13.172
"I have four lire," the villager said.

36
00:02:13.192 --> 00:02:15.412
"But it's not for borrowing.

37
00:02:16.253 --> 00:02:17.733
You have to sell me something."

38
00:02:17.753 --> 00:02:22.994
"But, I have nothing except my clothes and this book!"

39
00:02:23.655 --> 00:02:24.515
Pinocchio cried.

40
00:02:24.535 --> 00:02:28.556
"Then I'll take your book," the villager said.

41
00:02:29.164 --> 00:02:31.185
He knew the book cost more than four lire.

42
00:02:31.866 --> 00:02:33.747
Pinocchio took the money.

43
00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:37.910
Pinocchio ran inside the tent.

44
00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:40.272
The flute and drums played a new song.

45
00:02:41.092 --> 00:02:43.133
A few marionettes were brought out to dance.

46
00:02:44.034 --> 00:02:47.176
"Hey, they are wooden boys just like me!"

47
00:02:47.697 --> 00:02:49.117
Pinocchio said excitedly.

48
00:02:50.218 --> 00:02:52.079
He ran to the stage to look closer.

49
00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:54.861
"But wait.

50
00:02:55.322 --> 00:02:56.302
They aren't real!

51
00:02:56.743 --> 00:02:58.484
They are dancing with strings!

52
00:02:59.204 --> 00:03:04.546
I can dance better than that, and I don't need strings or a hiding man to pull them!"

53
00:03:05.266 --> 00:03:11.907
Pinocchio jumped on stage with the marionettes and shouted, "I am the amazing Pinocchio."

54
00:03:14.208 --> 00:03:16.689
He danced and twirled and jumped and flipped.

55
00:03:18.929 --> 00:03:20.350
The crowd laughed and cheered.

56
00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:23.551
"Yeah, Pinocchio!

57
00:03:23.931 --> 00:03:26.071
You're the best puppet ever!"

58
00:03:27.092 --> 00:03:28.532
Suddenly, the music stopped.

59
00:03:29.032 --> 00:03:31.934
A man came from behind the stage and grabbed Pinocchio.

60
00:03:31.955 --> 00:03:34.697
"The show's over, folks!"

61
00:03:35.457 --> 00:03:35.898
he said.

62
00:03:35.918 --> 00:03:41.142
"If you want to see the amazing Pinocchio, you have to pay for another show!"

63
00:03:42.043 --> 00:03:43.784
He pulled Pinocchio behind the stage.

64
00:03:43.804 --> 00:03:46.706
"Help, help!"

65
00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:47.987
Pinocchio cried.

66
00:03:48.007 --> 00:03:50.089
"Please! Help me!"

67
00:03:52.331 --> 00:03:55.233
Pinocchio was scared of this big man with the angry voice.

68
00:03:56.274 --> 00:03:58.556
"You are mine now, little puppet.

69
00:03:59.688 --> 00:04:01.729
You will make me a lot of money.

70
00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:04.451
A puppet with no strings!

71
00:04:04.831 --> 00:04:08.373
Ha!" The man began to imagine the piles of money.

72
00:04:08.393 --> 00:04:11.975
"Please, sir.

73
00:04:12.576 --> 00:04:13.817
I'm Geppetto's son.

74
00:04:14.357 --> 00:04:15.718
I need to go to school.

75
00:04:16.218 --> 00:04:18.940
Please let me go," Pinocchio begged.

76
00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:21.601
"You, someone's son?

77
00:04:22.242 --> 00:04:23.362
And a school boy?

78
00:04:23.782 --> 00:04:26.064
Ha! That's a good joke.

79
00:04:26.844 --> 00:04:29.627
We will leave town so Geppetto can't find you."

80
00:04:31.028 --> 00:04:33.130
The big man locked Pinocchio in a cage.

81
00:04:33.711 --> 00:04:35.993
He hid the cage under some blankets in his wagon.

82
00:04:36.013 --> 00:04:40.097
"Now, no one can find you," the man said, laughing.

83
00:04:40.898 --> 00:04:41.959
He packed up his tent.

84
00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:46.724
"Oh, Father, I'm so sorry," cried Pinocchio.

85
00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.204
"Please, save me!

86
00:04:49.224 --> 00:04:51.369
I want my father.
